  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 49,
  "sortOrder": 19049,
  "verseCount": 20,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Hear this, all ye people; give ear, all ye inhabitants of the world:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Both low and high, rich and poor, together.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "My mouth shall speak of wisdom; and the meditation of my heart shall be of understanding.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "I will incline mine ear to a parable: I will open my dark saying upon the harp.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Wherefore should I fear in the days of evil, when the iniquity of my heels shall compass me about?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "They that trust in their wealth, and boast themselves in the multitude of their riches;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "None of them can by any means redeem his brother, nor give to God a ransom for him:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "(For the redemption of their soul is precious, and it ceaseth for ever:)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "That he should still live for ever, and not see corruption.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "For he seeth that wise men die, likewise the fool and the brutish person perish, and leave their wealth to others.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Their inward thought is, that their houses shall continue for ever, and their dwelling places to all generations; they call their lands after their own names.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Nevertheless man being in honour abideth not: he is like the beasts that perish.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "This their way is their folly: yet their posterity approve their sayings. Selah.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Like sheep they are laid in the grave; death shall feed on them; and the upright shall have dominion over them in the morning; and their beauty shall consume in the grave from their dwelling.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "But God will redeem my soul from the power of the grave: for he shall receive me. Selah.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Be not thou afraid when one is made rich, when the glory of his house is increased;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "For when he dieth he shall carry nothing away: his glory shall not descend after him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Though while he lived he blessed his soul: and men will praise thee, when thou doest well to thyself.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "He shall go to the generation of his fathers; they shall never see light.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:49:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Man that is in honour, and understandeth not, is like the beasts that perish.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 49:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:49:20"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
